title: Daemon
kind: overview
aliases: daemon metafolder-daemon
summary: The background server that holds your repositories, answers the CLI and the GUI, and watches the files.

The daemon (`metafolder-daemon`) is a long-running HTTP server on
`127.0.0.1:7523`. It holds the loaded repositories — each one's store, under an
exclusive lock — watches their files, and answers the CLI and the GUI, which do
nothing to a repository's data themselves. All bodies are JSON; an error is
`{"error": "<message>"}` with a status code ([[Error responses]]).

It is local-only and single-user: it makes no network call and has no user
accounts; every request carries a session token only your own processes can read
([[Session tokens]]).

